To facilitate researchers in comprehending the performance of each method, we extensively gathered experimental evaluations on public datasets. As summarized in Table [IV](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2306.10561v3#S10.T4 "Table IV ‣ 10.3 Evaluation Results ‣ 10 Benchmarking ‣ LiDAR-Based Place Recognition For Autonomous Driving: A Survey"), we collected the publish year, method type, code, source of results, maximum F1subscript𝐹1F\_{1} score, EP[[273](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2306.10561v3#bib.bib273)], and runtime on KITTI Odometry [[262](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2306.10561v3#bib.bib262)]. Furthermore, Table [V](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2306.10561v3#S10.T5 "Table V ‣ 10.3 Evaluation Results ‣ 10 Benchmarking ‣ LiDAR-Based Place Recognition For Autonomous Driving: A Survey") mainly summarized the publish year, code, source of results, average recall (AR), runtime, and parameter size of learning-based methods on Oxford [[264](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2306.10561v3#bib.bib264)] and In-house[[12](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2306.10561v3#bib.bib12)] datasets.

F1subscript𝐹1F_{1}

The KITTI Odometry evaluations revealed that Locus[[196](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2306.10561v3#bib.bib196)], Gong et al.[[203](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2306.10561v3#bib.bib203)], BoxGraph[[215](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2306.10561v3#bib.bib215)], RINet[[221](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2306.10561v3#bib.bib221)], and LoGG3D-Net[[162](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2306.10561v3#bib.bib162)] achieved F1 scores exceeding 0.97 in multiple sequences. In terms of EP accuracy, BoxGraph[[215](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2306.10561v3#bib.bib215)], SSC[[73](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2306.10561v3#bib.bib73)], and Locus[[196](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2306.10561v3#bib.bib196)] exhibited the best performance. For the Oxford RobotCar dataset, MinkLoc++[[157](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2306.10561v3#bib.bib157)], TransLoc3D[[159](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2306.10561v3#bib.bib159)], and MinkLoc3Dv2[[160](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2306.10561v3#bib.bib160)] achieved an average recall (@%percent\%1 and @1) surpassing 95%percent\%. Similarly, MinkLoc3D[[156](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2306.10561v3#bib.bib156)], TransLoc3D[[159](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2306.10561v3#bib.bib159)], SVT-Net[[8](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2306.10561v3#bib.bib8)], ASVT-Net[[8](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2306.10561v3#bib.bib8)], CSVT-Net[[8](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2306.10561v3#bib.bib8)], and MinkLoc3Dv2[[160](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2306.10561v3#bib.bib160)] achieved an average recall of over 93%percent\% on In-house datasets.

